1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,733
With diabetes, a wound takes longer to heal.

2
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:07,767
That includes the wound from surgery.

3
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:14,300
A long incision means more skin to mend, and more chance of infection while it does.

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:19,933
Minimal access surgery uses a few small openings instead of one long cut.

5
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:24,500
A camera and fine instruments do the work inside.

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:29,800
For suitable procedures, it can mean less pain, a smaller wound to heal,

7
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:34,300
lower risk of wound infection and a shorter hospital stay.

8
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:38,433
A smaller wound gives slow healing less to repair.

9
00:00:38,533 --> 00:00:44,667
Before any procedure, our team reviews your blood sugar, medicines and general health.

10
00:00:44,667 --> 00:00:50,267
Your surgeon then tells you whether minimal access surgery suits your case.

11
00:00:50,367 --> 00:00:55,667
Ava Consultants and Urology Centre, off the Four-Lane, Uyo.

12
00:00:55,667 --> 00:00:58,800
Call the number on screen to book.
